  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "A Gu Master ordinarily has only one aperture from birth. Gaining a second aperture is treated as an act that defies that limit.",
      "chapters": [
        378
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "sys_gu_master"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "With A grade ninety percent aptitude, Fang Yuan reckons a second aperture would mean a hundred and eighty percent primeval essence, double primeval essence recovery speed, and a second set of Gu worms, sharply raising battle strength among the same rank.",
      "chapters": [
        377
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_fang_yuan",
        "sys_gu_worms"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "When Second Aperture Gu takes effect, a bean-sized green light is rejected by the navel aperture, hops to the chest, and explodes into a new aperture that looks both real and virtual. Lang Ya land spirit states that a second aperture gives great advantages to cultivators, and still greater advantage after they become Gu Immortals, while a third aperture would need a whole new recipe rather than the same Gu.",
      "chapters": [
        490
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "formed-in-the-chest",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "gu_second_aperture_gu",
        "char_lang_ya_land_spirit",
        "sys_gu_immortal"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Heavenly Court discussion holds that a second aperture gives Gu Masters a huge boost in battle strength, yet also means double the time, effort, and resources spent on cultivation.",
      "chapters": [
        1880
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "cultivation-cost",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "fac_heavenly_court",
        "fac_gu_masters"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "The ordinary first aperture is covered on Aperture. The Gu that creates a second aperture is a separate subject from this page, as is False Second Aperture Gu.",
      "chapters": [],
